WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.035
-Let's get to some news here.
Big news out of Washington.

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:05.572
Today, Supreme Court Justice
Anthony Kennedy announced

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:08.441
he's retiring, which means
President Trump will pick

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:11.344
his replacement.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.379
When asked which judge
he'll choose, Trump said,

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.415
[ As Trump ] "Either Adam Levine
or Blake Shelton.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.449
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:20.453
They're both a little edgy,
for different reasons."

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.122
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:24.657
[ Normal voice ]
After 30 years on the bench,

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:27.293
Kennedy is retiring
from the Supreme Court.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.729
He's 81 years old, so he's going
to go from sitting around

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.732
in a robe all day to sitting
around in a robe all day.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.800
So it's going
to be very difficult,

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.069
but he'll figure it out.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.504
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:40.472
So after Kennedy announced his
retirement, Donald Trump Jr.

00:00:40.472 --> 00:00:43.609
sent a tweet, and this is real.
It said, "OMG!

00:00:43.609 --> 00:00:46.512
Just when you thought this week
couldn't get more lit...

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:51.150
I give you Anthony Kennedy's
retirement from #SCOTUS."

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.886
Everyone who read that was like,
well, the word "lit" is ruined.

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:58.925
So now what are we going to do,
think of a new word?

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:01.561
Some more political news --
Earlier today, Trump spoke to

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.396
a group of young people
at the White House.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.532
At one point, he talked
to them about NASA.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:06.866
Take a look.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.268
-If you don't what you're
doing, find something else.

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:12.639
If you don't love NASA,
if you don't love space,

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.340
do something else.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.776
And for the people that do,
get over there and be with

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.211
the space cadets, right?

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:21.981
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.017
As soon as he said, "If you
don't love what you're doing,

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.685
find something else,"
half the room cleared out.

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.319
They go, "Oh,
well, I'm out of here

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:28.588
if that's the choice."

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.422
[ Applause ]

00:01:30.422 --> 00:01:32.425
Get this, it's rumored
that Trump might attend

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:36.028
the World Cup Final
in Russia on July 15th.

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:38.030
if he does, he'll spend
the whole time hoping that he

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.133
and Vladimir Putin get shown
on the kiss cam.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.701
He's like,
[ As Trump ] "Oh, no!

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.971
I can't believe this!
I can't believe what we have

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.505
to do. I mean,
what are we supposed to do?

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:47.540
I don't know.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.574
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:52.612
I'm so embarrassed."

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:54.380
[ Normal voice ] Speaking of
Trump, he's in a twitter feud

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.849
with Harley-Davidson since they
announced that they're moving

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:58.885
some jobs overseas.

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:01.487
When people heard Trump was
feuding with Harley-Davidson,

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.456
they just assumed it was
another porn star.

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.758
And you go, "No, no.
The motorcycle.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.126
The motorcycle."

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:08.428
[ Applause ]

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.929
Some entertainment news --
The new cast of

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:14.000
"The Bachelor in Paradise"
was just announced.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.035
When ABC asked them if they
could take off work

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.704
for six weeks for filming,
they were like,

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:20.906
"Oh, we don't have jobs.
What?

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.075
We'll be there tomorrow."

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:24.710
You guys see this?
Oprah made a cameo in

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:28.414
this week's episode of
"The Handmaid's Tale."

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.949
And this was fun.
By the end of the show,

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.583
all the handmaids had new cars.
-Really?

00:02:31.583 --> 00:02:36.722
Yeah. No spoilers, but it
was really interesting.

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:38.658
Guys, as you all know,
it is Pride Month,

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:41.160
and last weekend was
the big Pride Parade here

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.829
in New York.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.129
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:47.233
And celebrations are
still happening to honor

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.068
the LGBTQ community.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.670
Here to talk about
it right now are "Tonight Show"

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.473
correspondents Julio Torres
and Patti Harrison.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:56.108
Welcome, guys.
Thank you for being here.

00:02:56.108 --> 00:02:58.544
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:01.080
Thank you for being here.
-Hi, Jimmy.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.849
Thank you for having us.
-Yes, and Happy Pride.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:05.151
-Oh, Happy Pride.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:08.721
Happy pride to you both.
So tell me, did you guys go to

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.190
the parade this past weekend?
-Well, yes, Jimmy.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:14.527
But as two powerful queers.
we've heard a lot of complaints

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:17.931
from straight people asking, why
are there only Gay Pride parades

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:20.499
and not Straight Pride parades?
-Really?

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:22.235
-And you know what?
They've got a point.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:26.105
So we've taken it upon ourselves
to organize the first official

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.540
Straight Pride parade.
-Wait a second.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:32.177
Straight Pride parade?
-Yes, but we don't know

00:03:32.177 --> 00:03:34.547
straight culture that well,
and we wanted to bounce

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:37.516
some ideas off you first.
-Yes, because, well,

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:40.053
no offense, but you're
the straightest guy we know.

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:42.288
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:45.124
-None taken, yeah.

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:47.426
-So here are ideas
for possible floats in

00:03:47.426 --> 00:03:50.463
the Straight Pride parade.
-Okay, these are possible floats

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.532
for the Straight Pride parade.
Here we go.

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:55.535 line:0%
-Yes. Okay.
So, what about a salute

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:58.037 line:0%
to polo shirts one size too big?

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.672 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:02.642 line:0%
-That's interesting.

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.110 line:0%
I didn't realize they could make
a float out of that,

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.578 line:0%
but that's good.
-Yeah, we checked and they can.

00:04:06.578 --> 00:04:08.146 line:0%
-Oh, okay.

00:04:08.146 --> 00:04:11.851 line:0%
-We were also thinking,
a man and a woman on a date

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.819 line:0%
where the woman's method of
flirting is just that

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.723 line:0%
she lightly smacks his arm
and says, "Stop."

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:21.093 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:24.263 line:0%
-Very interesting idea
for a float.

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:27.967 line:0%
-Okay, or how about
a dinner party where the women

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:30.202 line:0%
offer to clear the table,
the men stay seated,

00:04:30.202 --> 00:04:33.473 line:0%
and no one is disturbed?
-Okay. Interesting.

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:34.840 line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.341 line:0%
Interesting, but it sounds
a little bit too specific.

00:04:36.341 --> 00:04:39.312 line:0%
But I see where going.
-Or what about two guys posing

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:42.214 line:0%
in a picture together, and they
are both pointing to each other

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:44.917 line:0%
in the picture to, I guess, keep
track of who all

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.186 line:0%
is in the picture.
-Okay, yeah, all right, okay.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.521 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:51.757 line:0%
I could see that, maybe.
-Or maybe, a couple having sex

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:53.259 line:0%
in the dark.
Did you know that

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:55.928 line:0%
straight people turn off the
lights when they're having sex?

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.863 line:0%
And the woman actually keeps
her bra on.

00:04:57.863 --> 00:05:01.867 line:0%
-That's not true.
That's not -- all right.

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:03.535 line:0%
One more.
What have you got, Patti?

00:05:03.535 --> 00:05:05.138 line:0%
-For sure. I got this.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:08.707 line:0%
Just imagine coming down
Fifth Avenue, a float

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:11.443 line:0%
that is someone karaoke-ing
"Come On, Eileen,"

00:05:11.443 --> 00:05:13.612 line:0%
while the next person in line
to sing submits

00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:15.915 line:0%
their song request
to the deejay and it is also

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:16.949 line:0%
"Come On, Eileen."

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.217 line:0%
-That's fantastic. That's
a good idea.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:20.719
Julio Torres and
Patti Harrison, everybody!

00:05:20.719 --> 00:05:21.954
I like those ideas.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:23.255
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:25.658
Thank you so much.
I like those ideas.

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:27.493
Make those floats
out of that, why not?

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:32.131
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.166
Stop.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.869
I read that a group of
shareholders at Facebook

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:40.540
might be plotting to get rid
of Mark Zuckerberg.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.307
And their plan would be
way more likely to work

00:05:42.307 --> 00:05:44.243
if Mark wasn't spying on them,
using Facebook.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:45.378
So, I mean --

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:46.779
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.213
And finally,
this is very exciting.

00:05:48.213 --> 00:05:52.351
NASCAR legend Dale Earnhardt Jr.
is my guest on the show tonight!

00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:55.788
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:58.390
He recently retired from racing.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:00.292
Now he's just the most
terrifying Uber driver

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:02.494
you could get. You guys,
we have a great show tonight.

00:06:02.494 --> 00:06:04.030
Give it up for The Roots!

